```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "unmint a wiki shell the worn face minted, a person's hand alone"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///engine.wiki.retires", "candidate"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/engine.wiki.retires"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/engine.wiki.retires"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.wiki.retires ~ the owner face's unmint; the record of leaving stays

`lares wiki retire <slug>` rides a session of the worn face (or `face=N`) opened by the cli hand, so a seat session refuses. The shell's catalog rows, its workbench's ledger rows and its slot and Keyhive bindings leave; its workbench folder steps aside by rename; the slug's realm label forgets the realm id; the canon bag and its files stay. Its effect records travel verbatim into one retirement record in the face's daemon wiki working layer before anything erases. `dry-run=true` reads the counts and writes nothing; a shell holding authored records refuses `wiki-not-empty` unless `force=true count=<records>` names that very count. A run that died midway finishes on a second run.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ dry · force

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`dry` params=`slug/works dry-run/true ~ read what would leave`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`force` params=`slug/works force/true count/12 ~ retire a shell holding twelve authored records`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ slug · face · dry-run · force · count

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`slug` params=`takes/slug needs/required seat/1 as/<slug> ~ the wiki slug`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ the owner face, by persona index; absent, the worn face`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`dry-run` params=`~ read the counts and write nothing`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`force` params=`needs/all-of:force,count ~ retire a shell holding authored records`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`count` params=`takes/count needs/all-of:force,count ~ the authored record count the dry run read`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand ~ a session of the owner face the cli hand opens; a seat session refuses at the socket`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · face-malformed · retire-needs-hand · no-face · system-bag · wiki-face-private · no-such-wiki · not-the-owner · wiki-shared · wiki-not-empty · retire-count-missing · retire-count-moved · retire-carry-unlanded · waking-floor · content-mounted-only · face-not-open · workbench-slug-bound

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[engine.wiki.retires slug/works dry-run/true]] ~ name the slug`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-malformed` params=`~ face= names a persona index`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`retire-needs-hand` params=`~ a seat session reached the retire; a person runs it`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`no-face` params=`~ no face stands worn`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`system-bag` params=`~ the slug names a house system bag`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`wiki-face-private` params=`~ the daemon wiki never retires`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`no-such-wiki` params=`~ the vessel binds no wiki to the slug; the local half still runs`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`not-the-owner` params=`~ another face owns the shell`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`wiki-shared` params=`~ the wiki stands shared; remove the shares first`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`wiki-not-empty` params=`cure/[[engine.wiki.retires slug/works dry-run/true]] ~ the shell holds authored records; read the count, then force=true count=`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`retire-count-missing` params=`~ force=true rode with no count=`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`retire-count-moved` params=`cure/[[engine.wiki.retires slug/works dry-run/true]] ~ the count moved since the dry run`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`retire-carry-unlanded` params=`~ the retirement record could not land; nothing erased`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`waking-floor` params=`~ the vessel still wakes`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`content-mounted-only` params=`~ the shell stands mounted for content alone`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-not-open` params=`~ the owner face stands shut`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`workbench-slug-bound` params=`~ another workbench binds the slug`>>
```

